  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 2 December 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nUrban and coastal style come together in this beautifully appointed, architecturally designed home. Set well back from the road on a private rear section, the property enjoys a peaceful position just a short stroll from St Heliers' iconic beach and village.  Understated elegance blends with quality detailing throughout the generous 290m² (approx.) floor plan. Oak floors, vertical timber battens, white shutters and full-length drapes combine to create a stylish and sophisticated interior.\r\nThe spacious open-plan living and dining areas connect to a louvre-roofed deck and secluded outdoor entertaining spaces. A stunning designer kitchen with scullery, Miele appliances and a statement island bench featuring a concrete waterfall end provides a superb centrepiece for family life and entertaining.  An adjoining family sitting room with a window seat offers a second inviting space to relax, while a separate office provides flexibility for those working from home. A statement gas fireplace and six strategically positioned ducted heat pumps ensure year-round comfort.\r\nFour generous bedrooms are complemented by two beautifully appointed bathrooms featuring vessel basins and extensive tiling. The spacious main bedroom includes a private ensuite and generously proportioned walk-in wardrobe. Two additional separate toilets, including a guest powder room, and a large separate laundry add further practicality for busy households.  Wired for security and video intercom, the home also offers excellent storage, internal-access double garaging and additional off-street parking.\r\nOccupying a 434m² (approx.) freehold site, the beautifully established, low-maintenance grounds feature private patios, easy-care lawns, a garden shed and mature trees.  Zoned for St Heliers School and Glendowie College, with public transport, the waterfront and village amenities close by, this exceptional home presents a wonderful opportunity for families seeking space, privacy and a sought-after coastal lifestyle.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
